  "course_summary": "ISEN 660 / CHEN 660, SENG 660 | Risk Engineering | Fall 2026\nInstructor: Nancy Currie-Gregg | currie-gregg@tamu.edu\nMeets: TR 12:45PM - 2:00PM | ZACH 261\nGrading: Exams [50%], Homework [30%], Project [15%], Activities [05%] — A: 90-100%, B: 80-89%, C: 70-79%, D: 60-69%, F: <60%\nTopics: Human Reliability Analysis (HRA), fault trees, event trees, failure modes and effects analysis, Bayesian network models, Bayes networks, Bayesian network development, scenario models, logic trees, Developing failure probabilities, Developing quantitative risk models, System risk assessment methods, probabilistic methods, uncertainty analysis, analytical risk analysis techniques, computational risk analysis techniques, quantitative risk analysis, qualitative approaches, risk assessment, risk management, risk mitigation, risk-informed decision-making, risk communication, component reliability, system reliabilities, system reliability, maintainability, and availability analysis, system designs, engineering solutions, engineering systems, industry practices, probability & statistics for risk analysis, elements of risk analysis, measuring risk, system risk analysis, case studies, applications\nTools: MS Teams, Canvas, WileyPLUS\nPrerequisites: Graduate classification",
